    "message": "Move the walk's order-dependent branches and _replan_journeys to Rust\n\nadvance_movement walks a second time, in order, when it reaches a queue\ntrip's replan or a person placed in a slot: it reads a copy of the\npositions it keeps up to date and takes event numbers as the Python rule\ndoes. _replan_journeys and _replan_staff_support_trip are a kernel per\nperson: a refusal says how far it got, and the Python step goes on from\nthere. Results don't change: tests compare whole worlds with the Python rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K4QyYRukuCLBerKa4UYj4y",
