    },
    "message": "Take the requests at once, closed requests and agent_is_at_* in Rust\n\n_apply_effect no longer refuses a person who asks a queue at once or a\nrequest closed in a Run's last minute. A world without a floor plan or\nwithout movement_v1 is read as the Python rule reads it. The queue walks'\nchecks of having arrived are kernels, and staff_position_snapshots too.\nRules that only ask whether a value is a str no longer build a refusal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K4QyYRukuCLBerKa4UYj4y",
